d and a scheduled income for December 25, which will be 600,000 pesos from ACME STUDIO","at":"2026-10-22T19:00:23+08:00"},{"role":"sol","text":"The ₱600,000 income from Acme Studio on Dec 25 is recorded and waiting on your Confirm to save.","at":"2026-10-22T19:00:32+08:00"},{"role":"me","text":"I want you to move all of the schedule income and expenses from Credit Card to Savings instead do note that Credit Card is a credit card not a savings account","at":"2026-10-22T19:03:04+08:00"},{"role":"sol","text":"Savings already exists, so I didn't create a new one, and I've noted that Credit Card is a credit card.\n\nNow, a couple of things I need to be straight about: I can't view which account an existing scheduled (planned) income or expense is assigned to, and I also can't reassign an already-saved planned entry to a different account. If you want those scheduled items on Savings instead, tell me which ones they are and I'll re-create them there. Which scheduled items do you mean?","at":"2026-10-22T19:05:49+08:00"},{"role":"me","text":"What should we make next meal to hit my macros?","at":"2026-10-22T22:00:14+08:00"},{"role":"sol","text":"You have about 696 kcal and 39g protein left — a dinner of boiled chicken breast and rice would cover it well. Suggested: 150g grilled chicken breast (~240 kcal, 45g protein) with 1 cup cooked white rice, and a side of pakbet to keep sodium low — roughly 500 kcal, 47g protein. That leaves you a little room for a small dessert if you want. These are suggestions, not logged yet.","at":"2026-10-22T22:00:29+08:00"},{"role":"me","text":"Can I also take my protein shake instead so my protein shake will be the weight protein or on protein powder, milk 2 tablespoon of basil and 1 tablespoon of flax what do you think?","at":"2026-10-22T22:02:12+08:00"},{"role":"sol","text":"The shake works great — it lands you at about 1,609 kcal and 136g protein for the day, just 4g short of your target, with 341 kcal and 3.9g protein still left. The meal is